  {
    "function_v0": {
      "doc": "Replacing the pauser is timelocked, and that is the point.\\n\\nThe pauser's veto over pending proposals is the only defence against a stolen admin key\\nduring the 48h window. While this was instant that defence did not exist: an attacker\\nholding the admin key would replace the pauser with themselves in one transaction, then\\npropose maximum fees and a new fee recipient with nobody able to cancel them. Timelocked,\\nthe sitting pauser sees `pauser_proposed` and can `cancel_pending`.\\n\\nThe cost is real and worth stating: if the pauser key is *lost*, rotating to a new one now\\ntakes 48 hours. That is the trade \\xe2\\x80\\x94 a lost pauser key is an inconvenience, a stolen admin\\nkey is an incident.",
      "name": "propose_pauser",
      "inputs": [
        {
          "doc": "",
          "name": "new_pauser",
          "type_": "address"
        }
      ],
      "outputs": [
        {
          "result": {
            "ok_type": "u64",
            "error_type": "error"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
